
December Prayer Letter
December 16, 2013	· by narcolapser	· Bookmark the permalink. ·
December is here! I’ve officially been in the mission field for three months now. And we are gearing up for an exciting end of the month and year right now.

Every year OM-Lifehope does a New Years outreach. All of our evangelism team is hard at work preparing for it right now. And they have asked that we in Dancelink join them this year as part of the outreach. We are very excited to join in. As a whole, 50 extra people will be joining in with us for the time of new years out reach. They are mostly part of other OM programs and are using Lifehope as a part of their program. One good example is the “Missionary Discipleship Training” or MDT. This is an OM group from Germany of young adults in their gap year. (A gap year is the year between graduating highschool and going to university.) Overall, the 50 extra people will be here for 2-4 weeks depending on their program.

We don’t know how many people will be joining us in Dancelink. We are hoping for eight or so to be able to join us. We will be preparing two or three dances for the outreach. One of them is the “Dead Come to Life” dance which we did for Halloween, and then we have a hip-hop piece that we will be teaching as well. The third piece has been left to me, which is both exciting and terrifying. I’ve been asked to choreograph a swing dance piece to teach and perform as a small flash mob in Birmingham. Swing dance isn’t my greatest strength but I’m lucky to have friends back in the states who are giving me advice.

Christmas is coming! Only 9 days away. There are a number of singles who either live on base or nearby and so don’t really have family to celebrate with. And thus the obvious solution is to be family for each other! So we will all gather on base and have a Christmas brunch and enjoy each other’s company all day. We will play games and talk about our family traditions. I’m looking forward to it.

A couple prayer requests:

    Guidance as I choreograph the dance piece for New Years outreach.
    Openness of the people in Birmingham when we have the outreach.
    Provision from God for the last bit of support I need. I’m still short by about 7 people.
    Peace for all of us who are spending our first Christmas away from our family.

If any of you have prayer requests that you would like me to pray for, please let me know! I want to be praying for you as well. I am right now, but I’d like an update to know how I can specifically to pray for each of you. Every month we have what is called a Prayer Emphasis Day, or PED, during which we pray for our field, other OM fields, other mission organizations, governments, our supporters, each other, the gifts God has given us (both material and intangible), and many other things. So let me know how I can pray for you and I gladdy will.

God bless, thank you all very much, and have a wonderful Christmas.
Toby
